{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449148-does-anyone-think-dominate-is-too-powerful-and-changed-it-to-make-vampires-immune","id":1449148,"title":"Does anyone think Dominate is too powerful, and changed it to make vampires immune?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-20T14:44:06-07:00","id":1449148,"title":"Does anyone think Dominate is too powerful, and changed it to make vampires immune?","content":"It's a pretty popular limitation in a bunch of vampire media.<br /> <br /> The Vampire Diaries had the non-Kindred rule (I know Originals were special), and I am finally watching True Blood on HBO Max where vamps also are immune. I must admit Dominate is extremely powerful just getting to 3. Even advanced powers are really boring because it already does so much levels 1-5. At 7 you get multiple people, at 8 you get unlimited range, 9 is all of your blood line. They gave so much power to the early levels there is almost no where to go but let you do stuff on a broader scale.<br /> <br /> Would Dominate be worthwhile if all vampires were immune? I think it would be fine for most games, but maybe not Elder games where you really invested a lot and then got whooped by combat elders. Anyone ever run a game with nerfed Dominate?<br /> <br /> In a Vampire Diaries type setting maybe start all Vampires with 3 Celerity, Dominate, Fortitude, and Potence as a base Vampire traits, then give them 3 points to put where they want so starting vampires don't get beat up by high school jocks. Drop the clans and give all vampires the same weaknesses. It might be a fun twist. Not sure how limited the discipline list would be. In V D's they had Auspex, Chimerstry Obfuscate (maybe can't remember) and Protean though they were rare gifts and the Protean was dropped quick in the tv show. <br /> <br /> Or I guess you could keep all the disciplines and clans and still give the bonus dots so all vamps are formidable at least, but I think it might be cool to run a game without clans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T16:10:04-07:00","id":1449153,"title":"","content":"I guess you could take a page out of Reqium and have to roll against a vampires blood points","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T16:36:53-07:00","id":1449156,"title":"","content":"VtM is its own thing. I would experiment with increasing resistance to Dominate before making vampires outright immune (VtR works as inspiration, but so does Presence). VtM has a much stronger social hierarchy than a lot of other vampire fiction, so Dominate being there to back it up is something to think about.<br /> <br /> It's also worth remembering that all vampires can run around with 6s in all their Physical Attributes (pre-V5) if they want to spend the blood on it. Even without the physical Disciplines, vampires can be superhuman in that sense. The physical Disciplines are just way more effective.<br /> <br /> Clanless can work, though you lose some of the differentiation between characters. VtR 1e has a Clanless rules option in the Requiem Chroniclers Guide which might be helpful for trying that in VtM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T17:28:52-07:00","id":1449161,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of it depends on whether your game is focused primarily on intra-vampire affairs, or whether interaction with the mortal world takes center stage. My games are heavily framed by vampire politics, and so making vampires immune to the power entirely would essentially render the discipline useless in many if not most situations. That said, I *have* gone through a lot of the disciplines and made <i>individual powers</i> function on mortals only, where I thought that was appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T18:53:34-07:00","id":1449162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449148-does-anyone-think-dominate-is-too-powerful-and-changed-it-to-make-vampires-immune?p=1449156#post1449156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VtM is its own thing. I would experiment with increasing resistance to Dominate before making vampires outright immune (VtR works as inspiration, but so does Presence). VtM has a much stronger social hierarchy than a lot of other vampire fiction, so Dominate being there to back it up is something to think about.<br /> <br /> It's also worth remembering that all vampires can run around with 6s in all their Physical Attributes (pre-V5) if they want to spend the blood on it. Even without the physical Disciplines, vampires can be superhuman in that sense. The physical Disciplines are just way more effective.<br /> <br /> Clanless can work, though you lose some of the differentiation between characters. VtR 1e has a Clanless rules option in the Requiem Chroniclers Guide which might be helpful for trying that in VtM.</div> </div> </div> </div>In VTR v1 what were the weaknesses of the clanless vampire theme? <br /> <br /> The all 6's thing is quite a bit of time and blood for a newbie 10th-13th gen, it would take a lot of prep.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T18:56:46-07:00","id":1449164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Legendre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449148-does-anyone-think-dominate-is-too-powerful-and-changed-it-to-make-vampires-immune?p=1449161#post1449161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a lot of it depends on whether your game is focused primarily on intra-vampire affairs, or whether interaction with the mortal world takes center stage. My games are heavily framed by vampire politics, and so making vampires immune to the power entirely would essentially render the discipline useless in many if not most situations. That said, I *have* gone through a lot of the disciplines and made <i>individual powers</i> function on mortals only, where I thought that was appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>For sure it's a big hit to Dominate, I was just thinking of the theme, basically V D's everyone started with 3 in Dominate so not a big investment on the vampires part with 3 free dots.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T23:16:32-07:00","id":1449171,"title":"","content":"If I wanted to run a VD type game I'd probably use Monsterhearts seeing as there's alot of baked in logic that just moving dominate around rather doesn't hit on... Hell I'd argue the whole Beast/humanity/path thing is probably at odds with how the VD views the system which is... MORE like Wraith or KOTE possession by your shadow/Po than frenzy..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-21T01:44:35-07:00","id":1449176,"title":"","content":"The problem isn\u00b4t dominate , the problem is that masquerade lacks opposed rolls<br /> <br /> My recomedation is to homebrew them like I do or if you want some sort of official rules use requiem 2ED clash of wills mechanics.<br /> <br /> There is a lot in requiem that can be ported to masquerade and viceversa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-21T02:14:03-07:00","id":1449178,"title":"","content":"The way I run things, Dominate is a hostile action. Using Dominate on someone is as acceptable as forcing them to do something at gunpoint. They'll remember, and they won't be happy about it. The fastest way to make a life-long enemy, that Dominate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-21T06:19:49-07:00","id":1449185,"title":"","content":"Never watched/read Vampire Diaries, but it would make an interesting twist. You could give all vampires the iron will merit by default, and/or edit it so that anyone with the merit is flat out immune to mind control. You could also try to resist with rolls involving willpower, the self-control virtue, or resolve or something. V5's fortitude can apply to emotional manipulation and mind reading through auspex, you could make a power for resisting dominate. Which version are we talking about?<br /> <br /> What I would do for this, I think, is make the target spend willpower to resist every time a vampire tries to dominate them, spending dots equal to the gap between your generations to represent the difficulty.<br /> <br /> But to answer the question in the topic title, no, I don't find dominate too powerful. It's designed to be a power imbalance, because the setting as is revolves around power imbalance and the abuse of said power. Dominate is one of the cruelest disciplines and psychologically screws over both user and the victim, and it's horrifying to wonder if your thoughts, memories and actions are even your own and how much of yourself is actually somebody else. The user may lose the ability to see others as individuals, lives with the itching at the back of their mind telling them how much <i>easier</i> it would be to just to bend people to their will with a word instead of doing things the long way around. They're alientated as they're feared, mistrusted and hated by those who they could control... while being victimised with the same discipline by their elders.<br /> Frankly, I start introducing harsh humanity losses for dominate uses. In V20 that's either &quot;planned violation&quot; or &quot;casual violation&quot; on the hierarchy of sins. Use it sparingly, or end up the monster it turns you into. (Doing it when you didn't inititally plan or want to, I'd put under &quot;injury&quot;, &quot;theft&quot; or &quot;accidental violation&quot;). In V5, I can be more generous.<br /> <br /> But yeah, if you want to shift the themes away from that, look into game mechanics related to mental fortitude, and maybe borrow from Requiem, which doesn't have generation to set the control boundaries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-21-2021, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-21T10:42:23-07:00","id":1449198,"title":"","content":"In the older editions Dominante was powerful but not game breaking powerful. In V5 maxed out dominate has the potential to disrupt games. Someone pushing a dominate/presence combo can make anyone obey their orders, no eye contact needed and even elder vampires are susceptible to it.<br /> <br /> My solution is to allow elder generation vampires to resist attempts to dominate them by permanently burning a point of willpower gaining immunity to the attacking vampire power for a scene. This only works if the attacker is of equal or higher generation though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-21T12:27:01-07:00","id":1449203,"title":"","content":"I don't have a problem with Dominate being powerful, when you think about it a vampire with Dominate and Presence is just the social equivalent of a combat build who has sunk xp into Potence, Celerity, and Fortitude.<br /> <br /> Yes there is an argument that social disciplines usurp the role play sections of the game for susceptible PCs, but I would argue that is due to incautious players rather than broken power levels. Vampires who are known Dominate users should be feared and handled carefully, just like getting into a fight with a combat specialist. <br /> <br /> There is no &quot;safe place&quot; for a vampire, only degrees of danger.<br /> <br /> On the subject of usurping mental control over a character being a violation, that is a slippery slope and one that often clouded by modern day morality. For instance would you punish a Dominate user when they use the power to get a suicidal person down off a ledge, or using dominate to prevent a fight that would result in deaths? Would you start applying violations for potence use because it allows you to restrain another character against their will? If so every parent who has used their higher strength to forcibly pull a wayward child out of harms way would like wise be at fault. Assigning a violation only works if you assume the victims know best, which in vampire they often don't.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-21T12:49:41-07:00","id":1449204,"title":"","content":"Remember that Lower gen vampires are already immune to dominate from higher gen vamps in pre-V5 vampire (the real reason Tremere lower their gen with path of blood).<br /> <br /> The amount of house ruling to approximate VD universe would be kind of insane. <b>Daylight rings for days! </b><br /> <br /> Clan-less games are easy since caitiff is already a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25664-gubenyochi","name":"Gubenyochi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-21T12:55:08-07:00","id":1449205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449148-does-anyone-think-dominate-is-too-powerful-and-changed-it-to-make-vampires-immune?p=1449203#post1449203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of usurping mental control over a character being a violation, that is a slippery slope and one that often clouded by modern day morality. For instance would you punish a Dominate user when they use the power to get a suicidal person down off a ledge, or using dominate to prevent a fight that would result in deaths? Would you start applying violations for potence use because it allows you to restrain another character against their will? If so every parent who has used their higher strength to forcibly pull a wayward child out of harms way would like wise be at fault. Assigning a violation only works if you assume the victims know best, which in vampire they often don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>---Cutting out a long paragraph about my interpretation of humanity, tl;dr: It's not about morality, it's about not being a vampire. Humanity is a harsh unforgiving path, and any act of violence, domination or selfishness reflected in the sins is inherently linked to the beast and indulging even slightly violates the path. I feel that vampires who want to act and think like vampires, as dominate will inevitably lead them to do, should get comfortable with a mid-low humanity rating or switch paths.---<br /> <br /> I would not necessarily &quot;punish&quot; a vampire using dominate to stop deaths. I count spontaneous emergency or second option uses of dominate like those examples as being either Injury (8), Theft (7) or Accidental Violation (6), depending on the specifics of the situation. That's a slap on the wrist. It keeps you at average human levels of humanity. At worst you level out at humanity 6-5, accepting that sometimes you have to do what you need to survive or get things done (like violating people's free will), but not making you a monster so much as jaded/detached with a <i>&quot;laissez-faire attitude toward others\u2019 rights&quot;</i>. I feel this is justified for such a character, There are humans in the world of darkness that will have a humanity rating around here.<br /> It's considered less of a crime than property damage. If it upsets the player, I'll offer plenty of opportunity to earn their humanity back. Or pick an appropriate path.<br /> <br /> As long as it's not your first go-to response for problem solving, and you don't run around using dominate to enslave people as pawns in your plans every single time, you're fine, just a bit cold and arrogant.<br /> <br /> If you're not on humanity, this isn't even a problem. Lasombra are extremely unlikely to be on humanity, and the Giovanni may not be either. Meanwhile, if I recall, Ventrue culture shuns the use of dominate where other solutions were viable (falling within reach of &quot;accidental violation&quot; 5 humanity, 4 at worst as a rule).<br /> <br /> (And the use of potence in your example may incur a violation, depending on exactly what's happening (injury, property damage) and why (selfishness), mitigated by potential altruism. Restraint is a physical altercation, which is an act of violence. Violence is part of the beast, doesn't matter why or what caused it.)<br /> <br /> In retropect, in V5 I'd give all this a free pass, unless the vampire is violating their convictions","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-21-2021, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T01:16:52-07:00","id":1449233,"title":"","content":"Speaking as a V20 ST, not really. The ability of lower-gen vampires to ignore Dominate limits its impact for most neonates---unless you are quite sure of your generation vs the target's (and few vampires can be) an attempt to use Dominate is often a shot in the dark. When it works of course it's quite formidable---but no moreso than a Gangrel's claws give them the edge in combat, or the myriad abilities of Thaumaturgy. And ultimately, Dominate is less flexible than Presence. &quot;Zombified&quot; servants lack initiative and eventually become clumsy and robotlike---less effectual in many ways than a willing ally cultivated through Presence. Likewise with the social disciplines, there's always the ultimate drawback that they are temporary---sooner or later, there is the danger of the victim breaking out of your influence and becoming a determined, vengeful enemy. Although many of my STCs command social Disciplines, it is not frequently used on Kindred for that reason. Practical concerns aside, there's also the matter of pride---Ventrue culture looks down on Kindred who must resort to supernatural persuasion. A truly effectual and skilled manipulator should rarely need to resort to such overt and vulgar measures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T17:59:57-07:00","id":1450242,"title":"","content":"I like Dominate *because* it makes older, more experienced vampires more scary. It solidifies the feudal power structure that defines the game. It's essential to the schemes of a lot of the Jyhad's major players. I haven't looked at V5 to see how the discipline works there, but for V20 I find it entirely appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T18:09:54-07:00","id":1450524,"title":"","content":"Ironically, in my Chronicles, I'd noticed my players usually slept on Dominate because, while it's great for dealing with Mortals, the fact that it's so unreliable against vampires made them loath to spend xp on it. While all powers are this way, to an extent, I really wanted to de-empathize the need for low Generation with my current house rules, since it's so strong, players tend to grab as much as they can get rather than focus on other Backgrounds. So I actually removed the Generation clause, so that Dominate works on any vampire, regardless of relative Generation (this also allows ghouls to Dominate vampires, though they do so at +1 difficulty). To my surprise, this hasn't had much impact on the game, using Mesmerize as written (where you need multiple successes to get someone to do anything that seems strange to them, and I always keep the Nature of the target in mind).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T19:24:08-07:00","id":1450533,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24241_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24241\" data-vbnamecard=\"24241\">Lynceus</a> <br /> <br /> That surprises me to be honest. I'm really just playing with the idea of making it human only based on tv shows for a specific game, so many of my ideas don't actually become games, just fun to work out, but Dominate is such a problem solver it's hard to imagine no one wanting it.<br /> <br /> When we had a thread where you pick a clan and only get clan disciplines I went with Ventrue Antitribu, read minds, control minds, survive the sun, what more do you need <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T03:57:49-07:00","id":1450563,"title":"","content":"Dominate is a very powerful ability, but it has a few limitations and most of it's abuse comes from ignoring those limitations. It's because I'm aware of these that I had no problem removing the Generation limit. 1, you need eye contact, and there are rules in V20 for how you can avoid eye contact if you suspect someone will try to Dominate you. 2. you have to speak to the target and this means that only Dominate 1 can really be used in any kind of real time combat situation, as other uses are blatantly obvious to any witnesses; and it should be noted that Dominate 1 is very limited in it's scope. 3, multiple successes are required to gain any real effect with it's powers (looking at Mesmerize, in many situations you could get 2 successes and have it do nothing). And as noted, it's very difficult to force someone to do something antithetical to their Nature. All of this combines to make Dominate a useful tool against non-vampires, but tricky with vampires. Generally you need the subject to be at your mercy, or at least taken off guard. Compare this to Presence lvl 3 which makes someone treat you like a trusted ally and all it really seems to require is for the target to be able to see you! True, Presence is less predictable, but once you have the target Entranced, getting to use Dominate probably becomes a lot easier (which is why standard Ventrue are actually dangerous). Really this comes down to your Chronicle- if your game has lots of dealings with mortals, and covering breaches of the Masquerade are common, then it doesn't matter if Dominate is mortal only. I'm coming at this from the perspective that, with all it's caveats, in games I've played in and run, the difference between Dominate as it is now, and Dominate that doesn't work on vampires, can be academic (especially if you're a high Generation vampire). Now you CAN build a character to use Dominate very effectively, especially if Merits are on the table, but I think that's true of most powers.<br /> <br /> As a complete aside, my Clan of choice would be Malkavian or Toreador- see trouble coming, get the heck away from trouble. I think Toreador gets the edge though because Majesty just ends fights, doesn't require a die roll on your part, or even an action- just spend a Willpower and laugh people try to roll their 3-5 dice of Courage against a very high difficulty, with failure forcing them to make fools out of themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}